-- title:
--   Two components of the j-chart of X₀(Np) modulo p
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$, and write $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbf{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. For $M \ge 1$, `modularFunctionFieldFull M` is the subfield of $\mathbf{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $\mathbf{Q}$ by the series $j(q^d)$ for the divisors $d \mid M$, and `chartAlgFin M p` is the $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra of elements of that field integral over $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}[j]$. The data are: a $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra map $\iota \colon$ `chartAlgFin N p` $\to$ `chartAlgFin (N*p) p` which is the identity on underlying Laurent series (hypothesis `hι`); a $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra automorphism $w$ of `chartAlgFin (N*p) p` inducing on `modularFunctionFieldFull (N*p)` the chosen Atkin–Lehner automorphism `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N p`, i.e. the selected $\mathbf{Q}$-automorphism interchanging $j(q^d)$ and $j(q^{dp})$ for all $d \mid N$ (the identity if no such automorphism exists); and an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$. The assertion is the existence of two ring homomorphisms $\theta_0, \theta_1 \colon$ `chartAlgFin (N*p) p` $\to k(\!(q)\!)$ such that: $\theta_1 = \theta_0 \circ w$; $\theta_0$ is reduction of integral $q$-expansions, in the sense that whenever the image of $c$ in $\mathbf{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ is the coefficientwise image of some $y \in \mathbf{Z}(\!(q)\!)$, then $\theta_0(c)$ is the coefficientwise image of $y$ in $k(\!(q)\!)$; $\ker \theta_0 \ne \ker \theta_1$ and these two ideals are exactly the minimal primes of the ideal generated by $p$; and for every $b$ in `chartAlgFin N p`, $\theta_0(w(\iota b)) = \theta_0(\iota b)^p$ and also $\theta_0(w(\iota b)) =$ `qExpand k p` $(\theta_0(\iota b))$, the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$.
--
--   This is the affine, ring-theoretic form, for the $j$-finite chart of $X_0(Np)$ with $p \nmid N$, of the description of the special fibre at $p$ due to Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur: the fibre has exactly two components, each embedded into $k(\!(q)\!)$ by a $q$-expansion map, one read at the cusp and the other through the Atkin–Lehner involution, and on the latter the degeneracy map to $X_0(N)$ becomes Frobenius. It feeds the later analysis of the Igusa scheme and of the minimal primes of the chart rings used in the Deligne–Rapoport level computations.
